        "original_id": "4b70e1cb-44a0-5521-bf46-9476585cedaa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Judy Clarke, Eric Rudolph, Ted Kaczynski, Jared Lee Loughner, Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, Tamerlan Tsarnaev\n- Roles: attorney, client, domestic terrorist\n- Events: plea agreements, anti-abortion and anti-gay bombings, Trial of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, Boston Marathon bombing, MIT police officer murder\n\nFacts:\n- Between 1996 and 1998, Eric Rudolph carried out anti-abortion and anti-gay-motivated bombings across the southern United States.\n- Eric Rudolph, born September 19, 1966, is an American domestic terrorist also known as the Olympic Park Bomber.\n- Eric Rudolph was convicted for bombings that killed two people and injured more than 120 others.\n- Judy Clarke has negotiated plea agreements that spared clients from the death penalty, including Eric Rudolph, Ted Kaczynski, and Jared Lee Loughner.\n- During the Trial of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, attorney Judy Clarke told jurors that Dzhokhar Tsarnaev and his older brother Tamerlan planted a bomb that killed three people and injured hundreds.\n- During the Trial of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, Judy Clarke also told jurors that Dzhokhar Tsarnaev and Tamerlan Tsarnaev murdered an MIT police officer days later.",
